2. PRODUCT MARKING REQUIREMENT  (specified Notice under CERN-OHL-S-2.0 s.4)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CERN-OHL-S-2.0 section 4 provides that "If specified in a Notice, the Product
must visibly and securely display the Source Location on it or its packaging or
documentation in the manner specified in that Notice."

THIS IS THAT NOTICE. If You Make or Convey a Product incorporating Covered
Source, You must display the Source Location as follows:

  (a) DIE / PACKAGE MARKING. Where the Product is an integrated circuit, the
      Source Location URL must appear in at least one of:
        - the die surface metal or passivation layer marking, adjacent to or
          combined with the GSys mark (see section 3 below); or
        - the package top-side laser marking; or
        - the package substrate silkscreen.
      The marking must be legible under 20x optical magnification and must
      survive normal handling and assembly ("visibly and securely").

  (b) IDENTIFICATION REGISTERS. The Product must report, through architecturally
      visible identification state, values that resolve to the Source Location
      through published documentation. See AGENTS-todo.md for the pending
      assignment of the GlobecSys JEDEC manufacturer ID (mvendorid) and the
      RISC-V International architecture ID (marchid).

  (c) DOCUMENTATION. Where the Product is a bitstream, a soft macro, a
      simulation model, or is otherwise conveyed without a physical package,
      the Source Location must appear in the accompanying documentation and in
      any "about"/version output the Product is capable of producing.

  (d) PROPORTIONALITY. Where You display attribution or source-location
      information for other parties, the Source Location required by this
      Notice shall be no less prominent than that information.

